MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Applicant must have directly applicable experience that demonstrates the possession of knowledge, skills, abilities, and competencies necessary for immediate success in the position. Qualifying experience may have been acquired in any public or private sector job, but will clearly demonstrate past experience in the application of the particular competencies or knowledge, skills and abilities necessary to successfully perform the duties of the position. Such experience is typically in or directly related to the work of the position to be filled. Qualifying experience would be demonstrated by 1) Assisting in applying Communications Security (COMSEC) policies, Security Program regulations, and procedures for Key Management Infrastructure (KMI) to ensure proper handling of classified material and equipment;
2) Reviewing information obtained from inspections and interviews to complete various COMSEC/KMI related reports;
3) Using COMSEC inventory, initializing and keying procedures, cryptographic requirements, destruction and accounting procedures, and/or personnel security procedures to support a COMSEC/KMI program; and
4) Troubleshooting communications problems in servers and phone lines to determine possible compromised information and tampering of internal components. NOTE: This information must be supported in your resume to be considered for the position.. This position is within the Work Category Technician &amp; Admin Support at Work Level II, Series and Grade GG-9. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Department of Defense website: https://dodcio.defense.gov/Cyber-Workforce/CES.aspx
